# ai-prototype-accelerator — Docker build context excludes
# Static scaffold file — do NOT modify when processing spec.yaml.
#
# Only backend/, agents/, frontend/, db/ (and backend/requirements.txt) are
# ever COPY'd into the image -- see Dockerfile. Without this file, `azd
# deploy`'s remote-build packaging step tars up the ENTIRE project
# directory as the build context, including azd's own .azure/ state,
# generated Bicep JSON under infra/ (can be 1MB+), and any stray debug
# files -- none of which the image needs. Keeps the build context small
# and avoids "archive/tar: write too long" packaging failures caused by
# unrelated files changing size while other tooling (preflight.py, test
# runs, etc.) is active in this directory (Alliant build, 2026-07-17).

.azure/
.git/
.github/
infra/
hooks/
azure.yaml
azure.yaml.tpl
.env.sample

# Root-level loose debug/log artifacts only (anchored with a leading `/`
# so files actually needed deeper in backend/agents/frontend/db, if any
# share these extensions, are NOT excluded).
/*.txt
/*.json
/*.md

__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
